# ---- stacked child builds (optional — ON is the default) ----
# A child ticket whose "Blocked-by:" parent already has an OPEN PR is built ON
# TOP of that PR's branch instead of waiting for it to merge, so chain levels
# overlap (docs/RUN-BUILD-GRAPH.md, "Stacked child builds"). The child's PR opens
# against the parent's branch and GitHub retargets it to the base when the parent
# lands; the merge conductor holds it as STACKED_WAIT until then.
#   1  = on (default)
#   0  = off: no STACKABLE line is ever emitted and STACK_BASE is ignored, so
#        every build is byte-for-byte the one this harness ran before the change.
# flags/stacked-builds-off is the same switch as a file, for a one-box kill.
#STACKED_BUILDS=1

